kens-county"],["ARC or PLC in Pickens County","/arc-plc/alabama/pickens-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 11 grids runs 75 years from 1951, and May to June came in under 90% of normal in 37 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle sat at 265% of normal for May to June and 36% for August to September. In 2026 so far, February to March came in at 55% on the middle. Grid 16069 had its driest year in 2007 at 53% of normal.</p>"}
